{
 "id": "y9-2-3-arrays",
 "label": "2.3: Data Types and Arrays",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "do-now",
   "label": "Do Now: Question 1",
   "type": "exam-do-now",
   "questionSetKey": "y10-1-1-l3-2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why do we use hexadecimal at all?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It is shorter than binary, so it is easier for people to read and copy.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A recap question from Number Systems: hexadecimal.</p><div id=\"donow-root\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-2",
   "label": "Do Now: Question 2",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y9l23-do-now-2",
   "validatorKey": "y9l23_do_now_2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Loops</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does Total &larr; 0 go before the loop?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>So it is set only once. Inside the loop, Total would go back to 0 on every pass.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From 2.2 Loops. Use this program for both parts.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Total : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Total &larr; 0</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Count &larr; 2 TO 5</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Total &larr; Total + Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Count</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Total</div></div></div><div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-do-now-2-a\">(a) How many times does the loop run? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-do-now-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Loops part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-do-now-2-b\">(b) What does the program output? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-do-now-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Loops part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l23-do-now-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l23-do-now-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-ext",
   "label": "Extension: Do Now Challenge",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "drill-y9-2-3-ext",
   "embedContainerId": "y9l23-do-now-ext",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Extension: Do Now Challenge</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\"><strong>Extension:</strong> finished the Do Now? Try these questions from Number Systems and 2.2 Loops. Stuck? Switch on <strong>I need help</strong> to see a similar question worked through.</p><div id=\"y9l23-do-now-ext\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "title",
   "label": "Data Types and Arrays",
   "content": "<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithm Design and Text Programming</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Data Types and Arrays</h2><p>Year 9, 2.3</p></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Today:</strong> every value has a <strong>data type</strong>. Then: one name that stores <strong>many</strong> values.</li><li><strong>You already know:</strong> DECLARE, variables and FOR loops.</li><li><strong>Activities:</strong> trace a program in a trace table, then write your own code.</li></ul><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">DECLARE Count : INTEGER. Why does the line say INTEGER?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It tells the computer what kind of value Count stores: whole numbers.</p></div></details>"
  },
  {
   "id": "types",
   "label": "The Five Data Types",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">The Five Data Types</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: which type is best for 3.75? For 'Y'? Why not INTEGER for both?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>3.75 is <strong>REAL</strong>: it has a decimal point. 'Y' is <strong>CHAR</strong>: one character.</p><p>INTEGER only stores whole numbers.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A <strong>data type</strong> is the kind of value a variable stores.</p><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Type</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">It stores</th><th style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">Examples</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>INTEGER</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">a whole number</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">16, 25, -3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>REAL</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">a number with a decimal point</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">3.75, 1.68</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>CHAR</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">one character</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">'Y', 'A', '7'</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>STRING</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">many characters</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">\"Mai\", \"Room12\"</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\"><strong>BOOLEAN</strong></td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE or FALSE</td><td style=\"padding:6px 12px;text-align:left\">TRUE, FALSE</td></tr></table>"
  },
  {
   "id": "types-check",
   "label": "Exam Question: Tick the Type",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y9l23-types-check",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Tick the Type</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is '7' a CHAR here, not an INTEGER?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It is one key from the keyboard, stored as a character. We are not doing maths with it.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/22, June 2026, Question 2 and 0478/23, June 2026, Question 2.</p><div id=\"y9l23-types-check\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "A programming data type used to store a single letter, symbol or number input from the keyboard",
     "options": [
      "Boolean",
      "char",
      "integer",
      "real"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "explain": "char stores one character: one letter, one symbol or one digit."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "A programming data type used to store any combination of letters and numbers",
     "options": [
      "char",
      "Boolean",
      "string",
      "real"
     ],
     "correct": 2,
     "explain": "string stores many characters, letters and numbers together."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "compare-types",
   "label": "Compare: Same Digits, Different Types",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: Same Digits, Different Types</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Both store 16. What is different? Which one can you do maths with?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>A stores the <strong>number</strong> 16, so Age + 1 is 17.</p><p>B stores the <strong>text</strong> \"16\": two characters. You cannot do maths with it.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">A: an age</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Age : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Age &larr; 16</div></div></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">B: a room name</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Room : STRING</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">Room &larr; \"16\"</div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "types-table",
   "label": "Exam Question: Choose the Types",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y9l23-types-table",
   "validatorKey": "y9l23_types_table",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Choose the Types</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is the telephone number not an INTEGER?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It has a + and a space. And we never do maths with a telephone number.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/21, June 2026, Question 3. Write the best data type for each variable.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-types-table-a\">(a) Age: the age of the student, for example 16 [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-types-table-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"types-table-a\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Choose the Types part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-types-table-b\">(b) TelephoneNumber: for example +44 7846398573 [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-types-table-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"types-table-b\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Choose the Types part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-types-table-c\">(c) Teenager: whether the student is a teenager, for example TRUE [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-types-table-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"types-table-c\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Choose the Types part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l23-types-table-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l23-types-table-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "array-why",
   "label": "Why Arrays?",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Why Arrays?</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: you need to store 30 marks. How many DECLARE lines would A need? How many does B need?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>A needs <strong>30</strong> DECLARE lines, one for each mark.</p><p>B needs <strong>one</strong>: ARRAY[1:30].</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">A: separate variables</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Mark1 : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Mark2 : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Mark3 : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Mark4 : INTEGER</div></div></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">B: one array</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Marks : ARRAY[1:4] OF INTEGER</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>An <strong>array</strong> is one name that stores many values.</li><li>Every value has the <strong>same data type</strong>: OF INTEGER.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "array-index",
   "label": "Index and Element",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Index and Element</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: what is Marks[3]? Is the 3 a mark, or a position?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Marks[3] is <strong>8</strong>.</p><p>The 3 is a <strong>position</strong>: go to index 3 and read the value there.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Marks : ARRAY[1:4] OF INTEGER</div></div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Marks</strong></p><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Index</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">1</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">2</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">4</td></tr><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Value</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">6</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">8</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">5</td></tr></table></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>Each value in an array is an <strong>element</strong>.</li><li>Its position number is its <strong>index</strong>. The first index is 1.</li><li><strong>Marks[3]</strong> means the element at index 3.</li><li>[1:4] gives the first and last index: 4 elements.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "compare-index",
   "label": "Compare: Index or Value?",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: Index or Value?</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict what A, B and C output. Why are B and C different?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p><strong>A:</strong> Marks[3] is <strong>8</strong>.</p><p><strong>B:</strong> 8 + 1 = <strong>9</strong>. The 1 is added to the value.</p><p><strong>C:</strong> 3 + 1 = 4, so it outputs Marks[4]: <strong>5</strong>. The 1 is added to the index.</p></div></details><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Marks</strong></p><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Index</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">1</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">2</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">4</td></tr><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Value</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">6</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">8</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">5</td></tr></table><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\" style=\"grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">A</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Marks[3]</div></div></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">B</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Marks[3] + 1</div></div></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">C</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">OUTPUT Marks[3 + 1]</div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "array-check",
   "label": "Check: Read the Array",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y9l23-array-check",
   "validatorKey": "y9l23_array_check",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Read the Array</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is the answer to (c) not OUTPUT \"Sam\"?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Both show Sam. But Names[5] reads the array, so it still works if the name at index 5 changes.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Names : ARRAY[1:5] OF STRING</div></div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Names</strong></p><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Index</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">1</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">2</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">4</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">5</td></tr><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Value</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">\"Ali\"</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">\"Mai\"</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">\"Ben\"</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">\"Joy\"</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">\"Sam\"</td></tr></table></div><div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-array-check-a\">(a) What does OUTPUT Names[2] output? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-array-check-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"array-check-a\" aria-label=\"Check: Read the Array part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-array-check-b\">(b) Which index holds \"Joy\"? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-array-check-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"array-check-b\" aria-label=\"Check: Read the Array part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y9l23-array-check-c\">(c) Write the line that outputs \"Sam\". [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-array-check-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"array-check-c\" aria-label=\"Check: Read the Array part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-array-check-d\">(d) What data type is each element? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-array-check-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"array-check-d\" aria-label=\"Check: Read the Array part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l23-array-check-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l23-array-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "array-loop",
   "label": "Loops and Arrays",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Loops and Arrays</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: Index goes 1, 2, 3, 4. What does this program output?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>6, then 3, then 8, then 5.</p><p>On each pass, Index is the next position, so Marks[Index] is the next element.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Index : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Index &larr; 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Marks[Index]</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Index</div></div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Marks</strong></p><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Index</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">1</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">2</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">4</td></tr><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Value</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">6</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">8</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">5</td></tr></table></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>The loop counter is used as the <strong>index</strong>.</li><li>Each pass visits the <strong>next element</strong>.</li><li>The same three lines work for 4 elements or 400: change the number after TO.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "activity-1",
   "label": "Activity 1: Trace an Array",
