   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Activity 1: Trace an Array</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does Total go up by a different amount on each pass?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Each pass adds a different element: Scores[1], then Scores[2], then Scores[3], then Scores[4].</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Fill in a row whenever a variable changes or something is output.</p><div id=\"y9l23-embed-1\" class=\"lesson-embed\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-temps",
   "label": "Exam-Style Question: Temperatures",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y9l23-exam-temps",
   "validatorKey": "y9l23_exam_temps",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam-Style Question: Temperatures</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is each element REAL and not INTEGER?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>The temperatures have a decimal point, such as 31.5.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A program stores the temperature, in &deg;C, at midday for each day of one week.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">DECLARE Temps : ARRAY[1:7] OF REAL</div></div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Temps</strong></p><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"margin:0 0 4px\"><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Index</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">1</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">2</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">3</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">4</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">5</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">6</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);color:var(--muted)\">7</td></tr><tr><th style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace);text-align:left\">Value</th><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">31.5</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">33.0</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">30.5</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">34.0</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">32.5</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">29.5</td><td style=\"padding:5px 12px;text-align:center;font:700 17px var(--font-mono, monospace)\">31.0</td></tr></table></div><div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-exam-temps-a\">(a) How many elements does Temps have? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-exam-temps-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-temps-a\" aria-label=\"Exam-Style Question: Temperatures part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-exam-temps-b\">(b) Give the data type of each element. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-exam-temps-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-temps-b\" aria-label=\"Exam-Style Question: Temperatures part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9l23-exam-temps-c\">(c) What is the value of Temps[4]? [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-exam-temps-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-temps-c\" aria-label=\"Exam-Style Question: Temperatures part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response is-line\"><label for=\"y9l23-exam-temps-d\">(d) Write the line that outputs the temperature for day 6. [1]</label><input id=\"y9l23-exam-temps-d\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-temps-d\" aria-label=\"Exam-Style Question: Temperatures part d\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9l23-exam-temps-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 4 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y9l23-exam-temps-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "exam-purpose",
   "label": "Exam-Style Question: Why Use an Array?",
   "type": "self-marked-response",
   "containerId": "y9l23-exam-purpose",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam-Style Question: Why Use an Array?</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">This question has 2 marks. What two ideas do you need?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>What an array stores (many values, one name, same data type), and why that helps (an index, so a loop can visit every value).</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">The program could use seven separate variables, one for each day, instead of the array Temps.</p><div id=\"y9l23-exam-purpose\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "array-purpose",
     "prompt": "Explain the purpose of an array. [2]",
     "marks": 2,
     "modelAnswer": "An array stores many values of the same data type under one name (identifier). Each value is found by its index, so a loop can visit every value with very little code."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "activity-2",
   "label": "Activity 2: Write the Array Code",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "drill-y9-2-3-code",
   "embedContainerId": "y9l23-activity-2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Activity 2: Write the Array Code</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why are the numbers in the array different every time?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>So your code must read the array. Typing the answer number will not work.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Write each program in Cambridge pseudocode. The array is already filled. Your code is run and checked straight away.</p><div id=\"y9l23-activity-2\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "plenary",
   "label": "Plenary: Data Types and Arrays Drill",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "drill-y9-2-3-arrays",
   "embedContainerId": "y9l23-plenary",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Data Types and Arrays Drill</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why practise with new arrays every time?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>If you can read any array, you really understand indexes.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Data types, what an array is for, reading an array by its index, and loops over an array. Your progress is saved.</p><div id=\"y9l23-plenary\"></div>"
  }
 ],
